# Question: on a daemon whose config defines no system/authorization/login-service
# section at all, is a local user with no login-service reference admitted on
# SSH, Web, REST, and gRPC with the correct password while a wrong password is
# refused on every door?
# Why a unit test cannot decide it: only booting a live daemon on an untouched
# legacy config proves every gated listener accepts an absent login-service
# generation without locking out existing deployments on upgrade.
#
# VALIDATES: AC-7 (OD-3 option a) -- absent login-service section admits user on every door
# PREVENTS: upgrade regressions refusing logins when login-service is omitted

option=timeout:value=60s
option=storage:value=disk
cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=le test fixture plugin/login-service-absent-section $PORT $PORT2 $PORT3:timeout=50s
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stderr:contains=OK: config without login-service section admitted user on SSH, Web, REST, and gRPC
reject=stderr:contains=ZE-OBSERVER-FAIL
